dsda-doom - authors, contributors and credits
=============================================

This file is the single place where the copyright notices and the credits for
dsda-doom live.

The source files used to carry a full copyright and licence header each, some
thirty lines of it. They no longer do. The C++ rewrite moves code between
files constantly, which made those per-file headers drift out of date almost
immediately and impossible to keep honest. Collecting them here changes
nothing about the licensing - it only puts the notices somewhere they can stay
correct, and it means nobody has to read 480 files to find out who built this.

The licence itself is in COPYING: the GNU General Public License, version 2 or
(at your option) any later version. Everything in this repository is covered
by it unless the file itself says otherwise. The files that say otherwise are
listed under "Third-party code" at the end of this file - those keep their own
notice in the source because their licences require it.

Each source file still states its own licence, in one machine-readable line at
the top:

  // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later

That is the whole header. It is enough for licence scanners and for anyone
reading the file, and unlike the old boilerplate it stays true when code moves
between files. Eight files carry no tag, because their terms have no standard
SPDX identifier and inventing one would be worse than saying nothing; they
keep their full notice in the source instead:

  gl_sky.c, gl_vertex.c          BSD-style, with an extra non-standard clause
  md5.c, md5.h                   public domain
  win_opendir.c, win_opendir.h   public domain
  xs_Float.h                     terms not stated by the author
  textscreen/fonts/normal.h      see textscreen/fonts/README

If you are listed here and the description of your work is wrong or too thin,
please correct it. If you are not listed here and should be, please say so.


